"[2412.20282] Invariance of intrinsic hypercontractivity under perturbation of Schrödinger operators (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.20282)\nciteturn1039view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.20282\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematical Physics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 28 Dec 2024 (【5†v1】), last revised 23 May 2025 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Invariance of intrinsic hypercontractivity under perturbation of Schrödinger operators\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Leonard Gross】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Invariance of intrinsic hypercontractivity under perturbation of Schr\\\"odinger operators, by Leonard Gross\nL14: \nL15: 【7†View PDF】 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:A Schrödinger operator that is bounded below and has a unique positive ground state can be transformed into a Dirichlet form operator by the ground state transformation. If the resulting Dirichlet form operator is hypercontractive, Davies and Simon call the Schrödinger operator ``intrinsically hypercontractive\". I will show that if one adds a suitable potential onto an intrinsically hypercontractive Schrödinger operator it remains intrinsically hypercontractive.\nL17: The proof uses a fortuitous relation between the WKB equation and logarithmic Sobolev inequalities. All bounds are dimension independent. The main theorem will be applied to several examples.\nL18: Comments:  | 124 pages, Accepted version\nL19: Subjects:  | Mathematical Physics (math-ph); Functional Analysis (math.FA)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 81Q15, 47D08 (Primary), 35J10, 35B20, 60J46 (Secondary)\nL21: Cite as:  | 【9†arXiv:2412.20282】 [math-ph]\nL22:    | (or 【10†arXiv: